    "summary": "blink-182's drummer from 1998, 'punk rock's first superstar drummer'. A marching-band snare drummer and jazz-ensemble kit player from Fontana, he brought rudiments, cymbal tricks and fills in single strokes into pop punk, moving between half time, the beat, double time and punk time inside one song: What's My Age Again?, All the Small Things, Adam's Song, Dumpweed, The Rock Show, First Date, Stay Together for the Kids, Feeling This, I Miss You. Then the Transplants, Box Car Racer, +44, the drum remixes with DJ AM, and records with rappers."
  },
